{
 "note": "Design round 9, feature paying (While the extra credits pay), the option chosen: pay-poison. rows are copied from the design's paying.json, verbatim (each row is the full HUD of build.cjs: hud4.js MIX.render on the situation's state with the fable-boss option, colour style, left-aligned, with the 1.0.0 frame; the hearts line's cols 0-35 redrawn by the option while the credits pay for a used-up 5-hour window). situations are the design's inputs: state is the engine's state. Kamal's picks (picks-r9.json): pay-poison. The row of the situation p-out (credits out, 5-hour used up) was drawn by the design with 1.0's green offhand sides around the empty well (the engine's paying() lights them while a window is used up, whatever is left), which said \"the credits pay\" when nothing was left to pay with; it is vendored with the 1.1.0 credits-out fix (src/hud/offhand.ts, design round 9's totem feature names the bug): its hotbar cols 9 and 14 are the plain grey side (a space on #5D5D5D) and its offhand edges, cols 9-14 of the XP-bar line and of the bottom edge row, the frame grey; nothing else in it changed. The fifth situation, p-share ($2.50 of $50 left: a share of 0.5, which the engine's rounding takes to 0, so the floor of 1 heart holds), is not in the design's file: its row was generated in 1.1.0 by the design's own build.cjs (round9/build.cjs, sha256 ba2380644843491ce6cfed66ef1a850fe03cdf5577f0a87616fdc6f214b3158b) with that one situation added after p-out in PAYING's list (the builder so changed has sha256 8431a8849795449551b8128428b16e6407fa76cb8661bfa09652cb2ebb2faceb); its other rows came out byte for byte as vendored. It anchors the poison floor in the design.",
 "source": {
