 },
 "id": "pay-poison",
 "name": "Poisoned hearts: the credits drain",
 "optionNote": "The idea from the design chat. While the credits pay for the 5-hour window, the hearts show the share of credits left in poison green (#8DB33A), the colour Minecraft gives hearts that are being drained: max(1, round(10 × left ÷ limit)) of them, the rest dark, so $45.80 of $50 is 9 and $4 is 1 (never 0 while anything is left). The skull goes while paying (the engine's own unshipped idea, day()'s absorb rule): the gutter shows the day symbol and the time to the reset instead. When the credits run out, the skull is back.",
 "title": "While the extra credits pay",
 "intro": "When the 5-hour window is used up and the extra credits pay, 1.0 draws a skull ☠ with the respawn countdown and ten dark hearts: it looks like you are dead and waiting, though you are working fine on credits. Only the green-framed emerald says that the credits pay. These options give the hearts row the credits' story while they pay. When it is the week that is used up, the hearts keep showing the 5-hour window; only the frame and the emerald say \"paying\", in every option.",
